@startuml 04_seq_optical
title Optical scan — frame-synchronous LED modulation (4-frame cycle, baseline)
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false

participant "OV2640" as CAM
participant "cam_task" as CT
participant "led_drv" as LED
participant "opt_task" as OT
participant "ui_task" as UI

== scan start ==
CT -> CAM : lock AEC/AGC/AWB,\nfixed exposure & gain
loop every 4 frames
  CAM -> CT : VSYNC (frame n) — LEDs ON since n−1
  CT -> CT : discard (transition frame,\nrolling-shutter mix)
  CAM -> CT : VSYNC (frame n+1)
  CT -> CT : keep as ON frame
  CT -> LED : LED_AXIS = OFF
  CAM -> CT : VSYNC (frame n+2)
  CT -> CT : discard (transition)
  CAM -> CT : VSYNC (frame n+3)
  CT -> CT : keep as OFF frame
  CT -> LED : LED_AXIS = ON
  CT -> OT : q_frames ← (ON, OFF)
  OT -> OT : D = ON − OFF (saturating, int16)
  OT -> OT : μ, σ of D (robust: median / MAD)
  OT -> OT : blobs where D > μ + kσ
  OT -> OT : track blobs; confirm if\npresent in N pairs within r px
  OT -> UI : candidates (x, y, peak SNR, age)
end
== optional off-axis test for a confirmed candidate ==
OT -> LED : next cycle uses LED_OFF instead of LED_AXIS
OT -> OT : ratio R = D_axis / D_off at candidate\nretroreflector-like if R ≫ 1 (threshold from E3)
OT -> UI : candidate class + evidence
note over CT, LED
  If E1 shows that toggling during vertical blanking gives clean frames,
  the cycle is shortened to 2 frames (ON, OFF) → 2× pair rate.
end note
@enduml
